explain (verbose, costs off) select pios1.a, pios1.b from pios1 left join pios2 on pios1.b = pios2.d where pios1.b < 1000;
                                                                         QUERY PLAN                                                                         
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Gather Motion 6:1  (slice1; segments: 6)
   Output: pios1.a, pios1.b
   ->  Parallel Hash Left Join
         Output: pios1.a, pios1.b
         Hash Cond: (pios1.b = pios2.d)
         ->  Redistribute Motion 6:6  (slice2; segments: 6)
               Output: pios1.a, pios1.b
               Hash Key: pios1.b
               Hash Module: 3
               ->  Parallel Index Scan using pios1_b_idx on orca_index_parallel.pios1
                     Output: pios1.a, pios1.b
                     Index Cond: (pios1.b < 1000)
         ->  Parallel Hash
               Output: pios2.d
               ->  Parallel Index Only Scan using pios2_de_idx on orca_index_parallel.pios2
                     Output: pios2.d
 Settings: enable_bitmapscan = 'off', enable_indexscan = 'on', enable_parallel = 'on', enable_seqscan = 'off', optimizer = 'off', parallel_setup_cost = '0'
 Optimizer: Postgres query optimizer
(18 rows)

